cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this harness in research on AI-assisted software engineering,
  deterministic agent guardrails, or provenance-verified code generation,
  please cite it as below.
type: software
title: next-expo-supabase-agent-harness
abstract: >-
  A deterministic agent harness for pnpm monorepos that ship a Next.js 16 web
  app and an Expo (React Native) mobile app over one shared Supabase backend
  (Postgres, row-level security, Auth), deployed to Vercel and to the Apple
  App Store and Google Play via EAS Build and Submit: Claude Code hooks that
  send the agent back to work when a check fails, security-invariant lint
  rules and pre-write guards, row-level-security isolation tests against a
  real database, cross-surface contract/parity and design-token gates, Expo
  config policy gates (ATS, permissions, plugins, CNG purity), an
  inline-citation provenance pipeline, and supply-chain-hardened CI.
authors:
